From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bron Gondwana <brong@fastmailteam.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 14:08:30 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Add DKIM2 Message-Instance support with always-wrap
 decoration

On lists with dkim2_message_instance on, record what Sympa changed in
each copy it sends, per draft-ietf-dkim-dkim2-spec-06, so a DKIM2
verifier downstream can undo the list's changes and check the signatures
of earlier hops. The DKIM2-Signature itself is added by the MTA.

At ingress (ProcessIncoming), before S/MIME decryption or any other
change: add m=1 describing the message as received unless it already
carries a Message-Instance, and keep the header block. It travels with
the message, base64, in the X-Sympa-DKIM2-Headers pseudo-header, so it
survives the moderation, held, auth, topic, bulk and bad spools without
spool-specific code; archive copies are stored without it.

Decoration on such a list does not edit the body: Sympa::DKIM2::wrap()
makes the original body, byte for byte under its own Content-* fields,
the middle part of a multipart/mixed between the header and footer parts.
The body Recipe is then one copy range whatever the body's encoding.
Signed and encrypted types are left alone. If wrapping fails the message
is decorated the stock way and its body marked as rewritten.

At egress (ProcessOutgoing), once per packet: check the saved header
block's top instance (never build on a broken chain) and whether the body
is still the one it hashed. Then for each copy, after every other change
and before DKIM/ARC signing: drop Bcc and Resent-Bcc, and add the next
m= with a header Recipe from diffing the saved header block against the
outgoing one. The body Recipe is the wrap's copy range, or none if the
body was not touched, but only if applying it really gives back the
received body; a body changed for any other reason (reception modes,
full-body personalisation, S/MIME signing or encryption, content
filters) gets a null body Recipe, so the header stays small. On DKIM2
lists the envelope/MDN tracking step moves ahead of this so it is
covered. Anonymous lists and resends from the archive strip the chain
instead, and the outbound signer starts a new one. Any failure is
logged and the copy goes out without the new instance.

Requires Mail::DKIM2 0.15 or later, loaded on first use. Includes
DKIM2-MESSAGE-INSTANCE.md (design) and t/DKIM2.t, which drives the real
decorate() and ProcessOutgoing and checks the output with Mail::DKIM2's
verifier and undo.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
